092 - This Is My Father's World
 / 
Key: D
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 92
Topic: God the Father - 

Verse 1:
[D]This is my [A7]Father's [D]world, And [G]to my [D]listening [A]ears,
[A7]All [D]nature [A]sings, and [A7]round me [D]rings the music [A]of [A7]the [D]spheres.
[A7]This [D]is my [G]Fa[A7]ther's [D]world; I [G]rest me in the [D]thought
[A7]Of [D]rocks and [A]trees, of [A7]skies and [D]seas; His hand the [A]won[A7]ders [D]wrought.

Verse 2:
[D][A7]This [D]is [G]my [D]Father's [A]world,
[A7][D]the [A][A7]birds [D]their [A][A7]carols [D]raise,
[A7][D]the [G]morning [A7]light, [D]the [G]lily [D]white,
[A7][D]declare [A][A7]their [D][A]maker's [A7][D]praise.
[D][A7]This [D]is [G]my [D]Father's [A]world:
[A7][D]he [A]shines [A7]in [D][A]all [A7]that's [D]fair;
[A7]in [D]the [G]rustling [A7]grass [D]I [G]hear [D]him pass;
[A7][D]he [A][A7]speaks [D]to [A][A7]me [D]everywhere.

Verse 3:
[D][A7]This [D]is [G]my [D]Father's [A]world.
[A7][D]O [A][A7]let [D]me [A][A7]ne'er [D]forget
[A7]that [D]though [G]the [A7]wrong [D]seems [G]oft [D]so strong,
[A7][D]God [A][A7]is [D]the [A][A7]ruler [D]yet.
[D][A7]This [D]is [G]my [D]Father's [A]world:
[A7][D]why [A]should [A7]my [D][A]heart [A7]be [D]sad?
[A7]The [D]Lord [G]is [A7]King; [D]let [G]the [D]heavens ring!
[A7][D]God [A]reigns; [A7]let [D]the [A]earth [A7]be [D]glad!
